{"content":[{"c":["OMEN"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Natural sign or occurrence prefiguring the outcome of a future event. Augury was listed among the abominable pagan practices forbidden to Israel (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.18.10","r":"Deut.18.10","rawR":"Deut.18.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.18.10","value":"Deut.18.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 18:10"},"). Balaam, upon seeing that the Lord was pleased with his blessings on Israel, did not seek omens as he normally did (",{"href":"?bref=Num.24.1","r":"Num.24.1","rawR":"Num.24.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.24.1","value":"Num.24.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 24:1"},"). The men of Syria looked for an omen to see if King Ahab of Israel (874–853 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},") would be favorably disposed to release the Syrian king Ben-hadad from captivity (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.20.33","r":"1Kgs.20.33","rawR":"1Kgs.20.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.20.33","value":"1Kgs.20.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 20:33"},"). Isaiah reveals the Lord as one “who frustrates the omens of liars, and makes fools of diviners” (",{"href":"?bref=Isa.44.25","r":"Isa.44.25","rawR":"Isa.44.25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.44.25","value":"Isa.44.25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 44:25"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Magic_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Magic_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Magic_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Magic"},"; ",{"href":"?item=Sorcery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Sorcery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Sorcery_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Sorcery"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Omen","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 18:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.18.10","rawQueryValue":"Deut.18.10","sourceRefExact":"Deut.18.10"},{"anchorText":"Nm 24:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.24.1","rawQueryValue":"Num.24.1","sourceRefExact":"Num.24.1"},{"anchorText":"1 Kgs 20:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Kgs.20.33","rawQueryValue":"1Kgs.20.33","sourceRefExact":"1Kgs.20.33"},{"anchorText":"Is 44:25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.44.25","rawQueryValue":"Isa.44.25","sourceRefExact":"Isa.44.25"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2a7e15884cca06821526251408962816678b73731b502878078a89d61e26cd57","sourceItemName":"Omen","sourceItemOrder":47,"sourceMember":"Articles/O.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Omen","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Omen","title":"Omen","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}